# Auth and identity rules

Authentication is a security boundary. Prefer Better Auth/core proven functionality over hand-rolled crypto/session flows.

## Required product direction
- Email/password registration and login.
- Mandatory email verification with OTP/code before sensitive product access.
- Secure password-reset link via email.
- Change email requires re-verification.
- Session list/revocation and sign-out-other-sessions.
- Strong MFA/passkey/TOTP for privileged/admin identities.

## Security requirements
- Never store auth/session tokens in localStorage/sessionStorage.
- Browser sessions use secure HttpOnly cookies; production cookies use Secure and appropriate SameSite/domain scope.
- Prevent account enumeration in forgot-password/OTP/login-related responses where feasible.
- OTPs/tokens have expiry, bounded attempts, one-time use/replay protection and resend cooldown/rate limits.
- Use constant/general failure messages where detailed errors would leak account existence.
- Password reset/change and sensitive identity changes should revoke or rotate relevant sessions.
- Never log passwords, OTP codes, recovery tokens, cookies or session tokens.
- Auth endpoints have dedicated abuse/rate limits.
- Backend remains auth authority for every protected request.

## UX
- Render localized Vimla validation/errors in UI; native browser bubbles are not primary UX.
- Unverified users get an explicit verification flow and resend flow.
